{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "B-1OWifeSULc0F8jX",
	"notes": "A rank-and-file member of the Custodian Guard: still individually the equal of a Chapter Master in raw capability, per the framework's Adeptus Custodes physiology section. Point total (physiology + oath + rank + skills, no gear) sits inside the framework's 1,200-1,600 point target for the Custodian Guardian tier. Equipment (guardian spear, Auramite armour) is defined in the Custodes weapons and armour files, not here. The historic Vow (Never Leave the Emperor's Side / Terra) is left disabled, per current post-Indomitus-Crusade Codex background; a GM running an earlier era or a Terra-bound Custodian should enable it (-10 points).",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "TXoDibzZX4gYkl5hA",
			"name": "Custodian Physiology",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Legio Custodes: the Emperor's personal bodyguard, each Custodian individually created rather than mass-produced from a Chapter's gene-seed, and never numbering more than a few thousand in ten thousand years. Chris Wraight's Custodes novels and current Codex: Adeptus Custodes background are the primary sources for this file; Horus Heresy-era material (e.g. Master of Mankind) is used for the Custodes' role and demeanour during the Great Crusade and Heresy, not for anything this file treats as a hard number.\n\nDesign: 655 (Attribute Modifiers) + 15 (Unfazeable) + 15 (Unaging) + 15 (Combat Reflexes) + 20 (Custodian Senses) + 25 (Regeneration) + 54 (Constitution) + 20 (Enhanced Move 1) = 819 points of physiology alone, before oath, rank, or skills - see the Custodian Guardian and Shield-Captain templates. This comfortably clears \"outclasses a Space Marine the way a Space Marine outclasses a Guardsman\" in raw point terms (an Astartes package is 563) as well as in the attribute targets themselves.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Custodes"
			],
			"container_type": "ancestry",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tWRTYa8rYQPbi0NRp",
					"name": "Custodian Attribute Modifiers",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A Custodian stands 2.5-3 m tall, built from infancy on hormonal and surgical regimes far more individually tailored than a Chapter's gene-seed batch process. Chris Wraight's Custodes novels (chiefly Watchers of the Throne: The Emperor's Legion) and current Codex: Adeptus Custodes background are consistent that a Custodian outclasses a Space Marine the way a Space Marine outclasses an unaugmented human - faster, stronger, more perceptive, and immeasurably more skilled from centuries of training against the best the Imperium has ever fielded.\n\nDesign: Framework targets: ST 40 (with the SM +1 cost break), DX 20 with training, IQ 13, HT 16, Will 16, HP ~50, Basic Speed well above an Astartes. Increased Strength +30 (B14, 10/level, 300) for ST 40; per B18's Size and Strength Table a creature whose SM matches its actual bulk gets a cost break on ST, and SM +1 gives -10%, so 300 x 0.9 = 270. Increased Dexterity +9 (B14, 20/level, 180) for DX 19, raised at the user's direction so a trained Custodian reaches DX 20, well above an Astartes' DX 16. Basic Move +4 (B17, 5/level, 20): Custodes cross a battlefield far faster than any human, matching the Astartes speed boost with their own greater Basic Speed on top. Increased Intelligence +3 (B16, 20/level, 60) for IQ 13. Increased Health +6 (B15, 10/level, 60) for HT 16, two points above the Astartes HT 14. Increased Will +3 (B16, 5/level, 15) on top of IQ for Will 16, matching the framework's explicit split between IQ 13 and Will 16 - a Custodian's raw wit is merely excellent, but nothing moves his resolve. Extra Hit Points +10 (B16, 2/level, 20) for HP ~50 (40 base from ST, +10). Increased Basic Speed +1.50 (B17, 5 points per 0.25 level, 30) stacks with the formula-derived Basic Speed of (19+16)/4 = 8.75 for a final 10.25 - well above an Astartes' 8.75, matching \"faster reflexes ... Basic Speed well above an Astartes.\" SM +1 is the framework's own figure for an unarmoured Custodian and carries no further point cost beyond the ST break already taken above. 270+180+60+60+15+20+30+20 = 655 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Imperium",
						"Adeptus Custodes"
					],
					"base_points": 655,
					"features": [
